From ddfd2c224e06d57fca944a87bf07d26d9b278144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 02:06:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: add the GPU BIMC_GFX source
 clock

The Adreno 540 on msm8998 loses all access to memory a few seconds into
every boot.  Any GPU access issued after that point stalls the VBIF
forever: RBBM_STATUS reads C00003C1 (VBIF_BUSY with PFP and ME both
idle), the CP never advances its read pointer, and no SMMU context fault
is ever raised because the transaction never reaches the SMMU.  The GPU
looks healthy at rest -- RBBM_STATUS 0x00000001, core clock at its
target rate -- right up until it is asked to fetch anything.

The cause is GCC_GPU_BIMC_GFX_SRC_CLK.  It gates the GPU's path to BIMC,
and no driver claims it, so clk_disable_unused() switches it off at
late_initcall.  That is why the failure is a function of elapsed time and
not of what is submitted: ring work issued from a5xx_hw_init() at ~1.4 s
executes normally, and the identical cmdstream issued from a delayed work
at 4.5 s hangs.  Booting with clk_ignore_unused makes the later attempts
succeed, and adding this one clock to the GPU node fixes it without that
workaround.

Measured on an LG V30 (US998), with a ring-direct indirect buffer writing
a unique marker to CP_SCRATCH_REG(3) and reading it back, repeated every
three seconds:

  before: iter 0 at 4572 ms: HUNG scratch3=00000000
  after:  iter 0 at 4572 ms: EXECUTED scratch3=01420006
          iter 1 at 7644 ms: EXECUTED scratch3=01420007
          ... 13+ consecutive passes, no faults

With the clock in place a full Phosh session renders on freedreno
(GL renderer: FD540) at 1440x2880, retiring 30-70 submits per second with
no GPU fault, hangcheck or recovery.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index 347706011..6990198e6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -1532,12 +1532,14 @@ adreno_gpu: gpu@5000000 {
 				<&gpucc RBBMTIMER_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_BIMC_GFX_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_GPU_BIMC_GFX_CLK>,
+				<&gcc GCC_GPU_BIMC_GFX_SRC_CLK>,
 				<&gpucc RBCPR_CLK>,
 				<&gpucc GFX3D_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "iface",
 				"rbbmtimer",
 				"mem",
 				"mem_iface",
+				"mem_src",
 				"rbcpr",
 				"core";
 
